# Causey core

Student competition discovery app. Chess is the working surface today; other types are not ready.

## Stack
- Next.js App Router, React 19, Tailwind v4, Zod, Supabase
- `DATA_SOURCE=mock` locally by default; Supabase when configured
- Scrapers live in `ingestion/` (TLA, CCA); do not invent new scrape paths without reading existing ones

## Early-build honesty
- Product is unfinished. Do not write copy that implies a polished, complete, or fully verified product.
- Prefer specific truth: "Chess search is usable; expect incomplete data" over empty "Beta" / "Coming soon" / "Live" / "Now available" badges.
- Site-wide status lives in the footer. Do not mount `EarlyBuildBanner` in chrome. Do not add decorative status pills above H1s.
- Never fabricate listings, fees, pathways, testimonials, or counts. Label illustrative seed data when it is not verified.

## Sources of truth (read before inventing)
- Design: `CAUSEY-DESIGN-SYSTEM.txt` + `app/globals.css` tokens
- Anti-AI-slop UI: `anti-vibecode-rules.txt`
- Setup / ops: `SETUP.md`, `ingestion/README.md`

## Defaults
- Reuse existing components, class patterns (`.field`, `.cta-enabled`, `.section-rule`, `.card-lift`), and tokens. No one-off hex or `text-[13px]`.
- External links: new-tab mark + aria-label.
- CTAs name the next action ("Search tournaments", "Book a meeting"), not "Learn more" / "Get started".
